7604,26,https://signoz.io/blog/opentelemetry-apm/,TRUE,FALSE,5,4,signoz github,"Running aggregates on your tracing data enables you to create service-centric views You can check out the SigNoz GitHub repo here: Best Practices for OpenTelemetry Instrumentation To get the most out of OpenTelemetry APM, consider these best practices: Automatic vs. manual instrumentation: Use auto-instrumentation libraries when available for quick setup Supplement with manual instrumentation for custom business logic Sampling strategies for optimal performance: Implement tail-based sampling for production environments Use head-based sampling for development and testing Handling sensitive data in telemetry: Implement data scrubbing in your instrumentation code Use the OpenTelemetry Collector for centralized data processing Versioning and upgrading OpenTelemetry components: Keep SDKs and collectors up-to-date Use semantic versioning to manage breaking changes Key Takeaways OpenTelemetry APM standardizes telemetry data collection across your entire stack It offers vendor-neutral, portable observability that prevents lock-in Implementing OpenTelemetry APM improves visibility in complex, distributed systems Native OpenTelemetry tools like SigNoz enhance the APM experience with tailored features FAQs What are the main differences between OpenTelemetry and traditional APM tools?",900,0,https://signoz.io/docs/cicd/github/github-metrics/,2,52,"Task: Evaluate if the source page should interlink to the target page using the given keyword and paragraph context.

